### Real-Time Synchronization Requirements

Implement or repair the appropriate real-time data pipeline.

When an important event occurs, affected dashboard components should update automatically without requiring a manual page refresh.

Examples:

- A new user registers → update registered user statistics.
- A user logs in → update activity and last-seen information.
- A user purchases a subscription → update subscription counts and applicable revenue metrics.
- A subscription expires → update subscription status and entitlements.
- A customer upgrades their plan → update subscription distribution and recurring revenue.
- A customer cancels → update cancellation statistics and applicable revenue projections.
- A payment succeeds → update payment records and recognized revenue according to the configured accounting rules.
- A payment fails → update payment status and applicable subscription billing state.
- A refund is processed → update net revenue and refund records.

Ensure events are processed reliably, with proper authorization, duplicate-event protection, and reconciliation mechanisms.

Do not expose sensitive financial or customer information through unauthorized real-time channels.

